   "tip": {
    "title": "Talking about the weather",
    "body": "In German, to talk about the weather, we use **es** (it) just like in English. We can say **es regnet** (it is raining) or **es ist kalt** (it is cold). \n\nRemember that the verb always stays in the second position in a statement, so if you start with **heute** (today), the verb comes next, followed by **es** or the subject.",
    "examples": [
     {
      "target": "Es ist warm.",
      "source": "It is warm."
     },
     {
      "target": "Heute regnet es.",
      "source": "Today it is raining."
     }
    ]
   },
